-- ── story 4-7c: the return-to-client document ─────────────────────────────
-- Generated by drizzle-kit (the two tables, the arm constraint and the
-- indexes) and hand-amended around the generated part: the fail-fast guard,
-- `IF NOT EXISTS` on every table and index (guide §3, linted from 0089 on),
-- the CHECKs, the client-scoped RLS on both tables and the post-migration
-- probe (drizzle-kit is blind to CHECKs and policies; `bun run db:generate`
-- afterwards reports "No schema changes").
--
-- Additive: two new, empty tables. No existing row or constraint is touched,
-- so the migration takes no lock on a populated table. No foreign keys
-- (IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE §3).
--
-- The vocabularies are pinned against their TS tuples by
-- test/client-returns.spec.ts: `CLIENT_RETURN_STATUSES`,
-- `RTC_ADDRESS_KINDS`, `RTV_BRAND_DOCUMENT_TYPES`, `RTC_LINE_SOURCES` and
-- `RETURN_DISPOSITION_REASONS` (the lines' reason — 4-7a's vocabulary).
--
-- RLS (4-7c decision 2): an RTC is the brand's own goods coming home, so the
-- portal reads it — the header carries the 0097 tenant + `client_id` shape,
-- the lines reach it through the 0073 parent-EXISTS shape.

-- ── 0. fail-fast ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DO $$
BEGIN
	IF EXISTS (
		SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.tables
		 WHERE table_schema = 'public' AND table_name = 'client_returns'
	) THEN
		RAISE EXCEPTION 'migration 0113: client_returns already exists — this migration has already been applied.';
	END IF;
	IF NOT EXISTS (
		SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.columns
		 WHERE table_schema = 'public' AND table_name = 'return_receipt_lines' AND column_name = 'open_qty'
	) THEN
		RAISE EXCEPTION 'migration 0113: return_receipt_lines.open_qty is missing — 0097 (4-7a) must be applied first.';
	END IF;
END $$;
--> statement-breakpoint
